{"schema_version": 2, "unit_id": "tag:006U:statement", "parent_tag": "006S", "chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "remark", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "There is always a bit of confusion as to whether it is\nnecessary to say something about the set of sections of\na sheaf over the empty set <MATH_0001>.\nIt is necessary, and we already did if you read the\ndefinition right. Namely, note that the empty set is\ncovered by the empty open covering, and hence the ``collection\nof sections <MATH_0002>'' from the definition above actually form\nan element of the empty product which is the final object\nof the category the sheaf has values in. In other words,\nif you read the definition right you automatically deduce\nthat <MATHSEG_0001>a final object<MATHSEG_0002>,\nwhich in the case of a sheaf of sets is a singleton.\nIf you do not like this argument, then you can just require\nthat <MATH_0003>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nIn particular, this condition will then ensure that if\n<MATH_0004> are open and <TEXTITOPEN_0001>disjoint<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> then\n<MATH_0005>\n(Because the fibre product over a final object is a product.)\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\emptyset \\subset X$", "MATH_0002": "$s_i$", "MATHSEG_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}(\\emptyset) = \\textit{", "MATHSEG_0002": "}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}(\\emptyset) = \\{*\\}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "MATH_0004": "$U, V \\subset X$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\mathcal{F}(U \\cup V) = \\mathcal{F}(U) \\times \\mathcal{F}(V).\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-confusion}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "math_text_regions": [{"region_id": "math/0001", "delimiter_kind": "inline-dollar", "source": "$\\mathcal{F}(\\emptyset) = \\textit{a final object}$", "source_hash": "sha256:46b1e513d60c438507e7737bf84e2df7da8f3eb37a75d28040156c5e63a7ebc5", "source_byte_span": {"start": 607, "end": 657}, "pieces": [{"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0001"}, {"kind": "text", "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001"}, {"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0002"}], "slots": [{"slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001", "source": "a final object", "command": "textit", "policy_entry": "p0-frame-sheaves-08", "slot_byte_span": {"start": 34, "end": 48}, "boundary_placeholders": ["MATHSEG_0001", "MATHSEG_0002"], "classification_witness": {"usage": "p0-locked-math-frame", "usage_source": {"before": "= ", "after": "$", "environments": []}, "source_label": "sheaves-section-sheaves", "policy_hash": "sha256:71d3aca14a16ed05f2eb0827d4ff6e145236bad3cff1e9e685dc675c059dd357", "anchor": {"source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "file": "sheaves.tex", "owner_tag": "006S", "owner_label": "sheaves-section-sheaves", "kind": "section", "ordinal": 1, "matches": [{"container_byte_span": {"start": 17631, "end": 18708}, "container_hash": "sha256:792139165e62cd6a503272e7c266371bf232620f144512476457b940aee7f5c9", "command_byte_span": {"start": 18264, "end": 18287}, "command_hash": "sha256:49a8a83e01427c662c8df564ef0a84ac03d1330c2e43a9366ae7c9fa32dd1a2c"}]}}}]}], "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:d7991f1d4c2b29ee50a31f05b8a584ac37aec9fa347714bf0be2c2397d076382", "source_text_hash": "sha256:29b52768d6d140e5953275362f82c6558d8484c5b775946a5b59689c448d7861", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:300359b7d5a4cb82aaef7ed72216c4e73c15f17e9ef80f285c651055a1a68adc", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bc38a46e5c42b6957cb818d7af55dab7822fd48afea902a554ae3fc46b8abf4d"}
